{
  "spec": "paladin-holy",
  "state": "written",
  "notes": "Written for the fork's healing sim (sim/healsim: the healer is raid player 0, players 1-4 its party, player 5 the tank). Flash of Light is the staple, Holy Light covers a tank below 40 percent behind Divine Favor, and the instant Holy Shock and a second Holy Light line spend mana only while it is no further behind the fight clock than five points (currentManaPercent against remainingTimePercent). The paced lines open when the mana bar is no further behind the fight clock than five points: a healer with spare mana reaches them often, and a healer short of mana only now and then (Holy Shock at a fixed threshold, with no pacing, healed less than the paced line). Light's Vigil (a party heal through the next Holy Shock on its target, 1340 mana at level 60) is in the engine but left out of this rotation: it lowered effective HPS by 2 to 9 percent in every variant tried, because the profile's raid pulses (300 damage on three members) are too small for a five-target heal that costs as much mana as almost ten Flash of Lights. Ranks follow one rule, stated in design/reviews/2026-10-08-healer-mana-audit.md: starting from the top ranks, a lower rank (never one learned below level 20) is taken for a spell when it raises the ranker's guarded score by more than two percent, the biggest gain first, the tank's casts and the party members' casts counted apart, and compared on the raid gear the ranker published for the list being tried. The engine states the client's own numbers for every rank with no downrank penalty, so a lower rank is a statement about this profile, not a measurement of the game. The site runs this list as written at band 60 and lifts every ranked spell to the highest rank learned below it. Here that is Holy Shock at rank 1 and Flash of Light at rank 4 on the four party members; every other spell keeps its top rank. The comparison is repeated on the gear each new list makes the ranker choose until no spell moves. Prepull Greater Blessing of Light (raid-wide): it adds bonus healing to Holy Light and Flash of Light that counts through each spell's coefficient, an assumption, since the client states only the amount. Spirit regeneration, mp5 and the five second rule are the engine's own formulas (the client publishes no spirit regeneration table). Every healer number comes from the engine's fake raid, not from a boss fight.",
